{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073481-do-some-mantle-effects-hinder-hiding-and-sneaking","id":1073481,"title":"Do Some Mantle Effects Hinder Hiding and Sneaking?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-04T18:24:56-07:00","id":1073481,"title":"Do Some Mantle Effects Hinder Hiding and Sneaking?","content":"Some Mantle Effects describe giving the Mien features like weird lighting around you, faint smells, temperature changes, small illusory objects like flowers and leaves falling around you,etc. But it doesn't seem like this hurts attempts to hide from others who can see through the Mask. why is this?<br /> <br /> Are the Mantle Effects only percievable if the Changeling is within your sight range or something? Or are there penalties to hiding from other Fae that I don't know about? I know that more powerful Changelings attract more Fae attention, so is the obviousness of their Mantles part of the reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T18:31:37-07:00","id":1073486,"title":"","content":"I remember something from the Pledge preview that Bargains make Huntsment perceive the changeling as a 'natural' fae of this side of the world, not an escapee from Arcadia. Effectively hiding in plain sight.<br /> <br /> Powerful changelings being more easily noticed by the Gentry has to do with the changeling's Wyrd trait, representing her 'gravity' in the Wyrd. Or at least, that seemed to be the case in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T18:31:56-07:00","id":1073487,"title":"","content":"At the moment, I'm tending toward the idea that your Mantle effects are only perceived if they're aware of your presence. You jump out to scare someone, and suddenly it's Halloween.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T19:14:11-07:00","id":1073497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073481-do-some-mantle-effects-hinder-hiding-and-sneaking?p=1073487#post1073487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the moment, I'm tending toward the idea that your Mantle effects are only perceived if they're aware of your presence. You jump out to scare someone, and suddenly it's Halloween.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That settles it, my next Changeling is going to somehow incorporate a running loop of &quot;This is Halloween&quot; into his Mien.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on a more serious note, what does aware of their presence mean? If you have good reason to suspect an Autumn Courtier is hiding in a box in the same room as you (and they actually are), do you suddenly start seeing autumn leaves swirling around the box or something? Or does that only happen if they loudly sneeze and reveal their hiding place?<br /> <br /> Edit: this is so going in the forum quotes thread","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:23:43-07:00","id":1073760,"title":"","content":"Your Mantle doesn't interfere with stealth, no. At least, not in 1e. Maybe that'll change in 2e, but I sincerely doubt it. Your mantle is in tune with your fae self, so it wouldn't give you away, though it might stylize things that <i>would</i> give you away. For example, an Autumn Courtier leaving dusty fingerprints, or a Spring Courtier's perfume carrying the scent of a fresh rainfall.<br /> <br /> Your Mantle is just an aesthetic thing that colours the rest of your mien. It flares brilliantly when you do something magical (and, even then, only in keeping with that magic; turning invisible might cause a chilly breeze to make someone shiver but it wouldn't alert them that you're there) but, otherwise, only exists to flavour your actions and indicate to others how deeply you've connected yourself to your protecting patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T09:52:25-07:00","id":1073777,"title":"","content":"Mantle is meant to build atmosphere and provide a small selection of benefits, and it costs Merit dots. I don't think it would be fair to have it break stealth automatically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T10:33:02-07:00","id":1073790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1073481-do-some-mantle-effects-hinder-hiding-and-sneaking?p=1073777#post1073777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mantle is meant to build atmosphere and provide a small selection of benefits, and it costs Merit dots. I don't think it would be fair to have it break stealth automatically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thank you. It's nice to see a producer taking interest in my little thread.<br /> <br /> Just wanna clarify to everyone that I know why it shouldn't hurt sneaking, just not why it doesn't. I'm a Watsonian by nature and for entertainment. I love talking about in-universe reasons for stuff and world-building. So this is more of a world-building/flavor issue for me than a mechanics one.<br /> <br /> I like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a> 's explanation, and I find humor in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10118\" data-vbnamecard=\"10118\">BronzeDog</a>'s explanation. Though if it's that dramatic, I might restrict that to higher-dot Mantles. Like ... Mantle 3+, maybe?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T16:06:20-07:00","id":1074375,"title":"","content":"Mantles could be consciously or subconsciously controlled; someone who usually gives off flares of light might darken when they're focused on sneaking (or on other things). It could also just be something a character figures out how to compensate for, as an extension of body awareness; if you know you're bright, bring a blanket and throw it over yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T16:19:29-07:00","id":1074385,"title":"","content":"i always thought the light wasn't something that emanated from you, but more that everything looked brighter and more vibrant around you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T09:06:36-07:00","id":1074683,"title":"","content":"It was an example; I'm sure there exist mantles with literal light (Summer Court giving off little static lightning or sparkler sparks, Silver Court giving off a slight glow, Film Court giving off lens flares), as well as ones where it's a perception thing. Either way, subconscious suppression or compensation still works as an in-universe reasoning.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Mantles shift based on the bearer; an unsubtle Summer Courtier gets little lightning flashes, a more sneaky one gets the feeling of menace around them (harder to notice).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}